## Scope

This increment exposes the already-proven current universal provenance of the selected persisted `Custom + Validated` challenger in the real Profiles UI. It is presentation-only: no History authority, candidate-space construction, GameIdentity inference, Auto Tuner mode inference, validation, winner selection, mutation or universal persistence was moved into WPF.

## Permanent production changes

### Pure presenter

Added `src/FFPerformanceEngine.App/UniversalProfileProvenancePresentation.cs`.

`UniversalProfileProvenancePresentation.FromProjection(...)` maps only an already-proven `UniversalValidatedProfileProjection` into display data:

- `IsVisible`;
- exact `GameId`;
- exact `AdapterId`;
- deterministic `key = value` lines copied from the exact `UniversalTuningCandidate.Values` dictionary.

`null` maps to a hidden presentation with empty identifiers and zero candidate lines. No placeholder values are fabricated.

### Profiles UI

`ProfilesPage.xaml` adds `UniversalProvenanceCard` inside the existing challenge card. It is `Collapsed` by default and has empty identity/candidate text controls.

`ProfilesPage.xaml.cs`:

- refreshes this card for the selected `Custom + Validated` challenger;
- calls only `App.Services.ResolveCurrentUniversalValidatedProfileProvenanceAsync(selectedCustom.Id)`;
- immediately hides/clears old provenance while a new selection is being resolved;
- uses `_universalProvenanceRevision` to reject stale async results after rapid selection changes;
- shows exact `GameId`, exact `AdapterId` and the presenter-provided exact candidate lines only when application provenance exists;
- keeps the existing challenge, A/B, historical validation and profile application flows intact.

